#
# Sourced by run-scenario.sh after prober_resolve and before the conf is
# rendered.
#
# The probe directive and the zone it is pointed at. NOT testkit's
# `test_ref_probe`: that aims ngx_test_probe_json() at the ref module's own
# zone, which is NULL in this scenario. A NULL zone matters twice here --
# zone_render is skipped (so none of our fields render) AND, decisively,
# ngx_test_probe_arm() only dispatches to fault_set when a zone is present, so
# every `fault_slab=` query would fall through to the (unregistered)
# fault_set_global and be refused. The scenario would then run green against a
# server that was never armed. cache_turbo's own directive passes OUR
# ngx_shm_zone_t and is what makes the arm reach the hook.
#
# PROBER_PROBE_ZONE is empty: the zone is declared by `cache_turbo_zone` in the
# conf (it needs a name the /cached/ location also references), not by a
# probe-side directive. lib.sh documents empty as legitimate for exactly this.
PROBER_PROBE='cache_turbo_probe ct;'
